<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33001" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕξις</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>formed by</i> or
				<i>forming habit</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ βέβαιον καὶ
				ἑ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				3.138
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. δύναμις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.149
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιεῖν τι ἑκτικόν</span> to do
			a thing <i>as a matter of habit, easily</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				2.18.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. πρὸς τὴν τέχνην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Damocr.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.1001
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>
			<i>from habit, easily, fluently</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράμματα ἀναγινώσκειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Artem.
					1.53
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				3.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.802f
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Epict.</u>
					3.24.78
				</span></i>
			; but also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. διαμένειν
			[λίθον</span>] remain <i>fixed in its nature</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				4.20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. αἴτια</span>
			<i>sustaining</i> causes, <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.273
			</span></i> (s.v.l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>capable of</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύσις τινὸς
			ἑ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ir.</u>
				p.14
			</span></i> W. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>hectic, consumptive</i>, f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				920b27
			</span></i>; offevers, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.315
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				1.88
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφυγμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					8.460
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					10.603
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
